    "result_text": "All 272 tests pass, including the new `createOwnerSetsRegistrationDateTotoday` test (the OwnerRestControllerV1Tests count went from 25 to 26).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the change so that a newly created owner without a registration date gets today's date, returned as an ISO `registrationDate` field.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `Owner` response schema, alongside the existing server-computed fields (`displayName`, `initials`). The generator produces a `LocalDate` DTO field serialized as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` DATE column, with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 When a new owner has no registration date, it's set to `LocalDate.now()` (only on creation, guarded by `owner.isNew()`).\n\n4. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\n5. **Test** \u2014 Added `createOwnerSetsRegistrationDateTotoday` verifying the POST response returns today's date.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` picks up the new field automatically (same name/type on both sides), so no mapper change was needed. The full suite (272 tests) is green.",
